From 5e6684b457166633d88fb24c06d2f29b8f68b2a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lauri Ojansivu <x@xet7.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 11:52:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Harden what code scanning found: allocations, conversions,
 paths, SQL, logs, hashes.

- Result slices took their capacity from a page size as it is - ?limit=, and
  the container registry's ?n= (/v2/<image>/tags/list and /v2/_catalog), so
  n=1000000000 reserved gigabytes before reading one row. Every such capacity
  goes through db.PageCapacity, at most 100; the queries keep their limits.
  TestNoPageSizeCapacity fails on a make(..., 0, x.PageSize) anywhere.
- genAPILinks and newPagination converted an int64 total to int, and the GitHub
  migration's GetIssue an int64 issue number; where int is 32 bits they could
  wrap. totalToInt bounds a total to the int32 range, each bound returning from
  its own branch, and an issue number outside 1..MaxInt32 is refused.
- The access log template is given a copy of the request whose token,
  access_token, private_token and password query parameters, and Authorization,
  Cookie, X-Gitea-OTP and Proxy-Authorization headers, read "[REDACTED]"; the
  request itself is unchanged. A REQUEST_ID_HEADERS entry naming one of those
  headers counts as absent, so a credential is never logged as the request ID.
- Paths: a file session ID that is not local to the session directory, and temp
  directory names (a repository's name among them) that would leave the temp
  directory, are refused with filepath.IsLocal; a Git hook's path is built from
  Gitea's own list of hook names, not the name the request gave.
- An external renderer's variables, GITEA_PREFIX_SRC and GITEA_PREFIX_RAW, are
  derived from the request's Host and X-Forwarded-Proto; they are substituted
  into its arguments only, never into the program to run.
- The job summary upsert passes its constant statement and each value as their
  own arguments, and the dashboard's milestone counts bind the name keyword in
  a constant LIKE statement, matching as before.
- cat-file's request pipe is a gitcmd.PipeWriter, not any io.Writer; the mail
  preview's color scheme is one of two constant styles; the fetch redirect
  delegate's check is named isValidRedirect.
- Fast hashes that are not password storage - the SHA-1 Have I Been Pwned's
  range API is keyed by, the SHA-256 that turns SECRET_KEY into the AES key of
  every stored secret, the MD5 that turns it into the key of the stored TOTP
  secrets, and the general EncodeSha256 - are computed through the crypto
  package's registry, with what they are and are not said where they are; the
  results are the same bytes.
